research/
*.log
.DS_Store
.emrg/

# `*.log` above is for the repository root (stray tool output). Manuscript run logs are a
# deliverable — quality-bar item 4 and the submission checklist require "scripts, data, logs
# committed with the manuscript" — and the editor's heavy-repro downgrade at triage replaces
# running the code with *reading the submitted logs*. So re-include logs under papers/.
# `research/` stays excluded regardless: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# is excluded, so a log inside the workspace remains ignored.
!papers/**/*.log

# A corpus or input a recompute reads lives under `papers/issue-<N>/refs/` — or wherever the
# package names it and commits it — and never in `research/`, because the workspace is excluded
# here and the verifier's tree is an export of the head: it carries the tracked files and neither
# `.git` nor any ignored path, so an input left in the workspace is not merely uncommitted, it is
# absent from the reader's tree (README.md quality-bar item 5, and the submission checklist's spec
# item, which is where an author acts on it).
